evated cholesterol levels.\",2\r\n6061,INHIBIDORES DE PCSK9,Los inhibidores de PCSK9 son una clase de medicamentos que ayudan a reducir los niveles de colesterol LDL en pacientes que no logran el control adecuado con estatinas.,2\r\n6111,AACE/ACE,\"The AACE/ACE refers to the American Association of Clinical Endocrinology and the American College of Endocrinology, organizations that provide guidelines for managing dyslipidemia and cardiovascular disease.\",1\r\n6059,DEFICIT FAMILIAR DE APOPROTEÍNA B-100,\"Este trastorno autosómico dominante es una fenocopia de la hipercolesterolemia familiar, causado por una mutación que afecta la afinidad de la LDL por su receptor.\",1\r\n6060,EZETIMIBA,\"Ezetimiba is a medication that can be added to statins to help achieve LDL cholesterol goals. It works by inhibiting the absorption of cholesterol and phytosterols in the intestine, making it primarily effective in lowering LDL cholesterol levels.\",1\r\n6063,SENSIBILIDAD A LA INSULINA,\"La sensibilidad a la insulina se refiere a la capacidad del cuerpo para responder a la insulina, y su disminución está relacionada con la dislipidemia aterogénica.\",1\r\n6109,ÁCIDO NICOTÍNICO,\"Ácido nicotínico, also known as nicotinic acid, is a medication that has been utilized for over 40 years in the treatment of dyslipidemia. It primarily functions by decreasing the production and release of very low-density lipoprotein (VLDL), which is crucial for managing lipid levels in the body. Additionally, nicotinic acid can be used in conjunction with fibrates to effectively lower triglyceride levels, further supporting its role in lipid management.\",1\r\n6113,HIPERLIPIDEMIA,\"Hiperlipidemia refers to elevated levels of lipids in the blood, which is a condition treated with various medications including statins and fibrates.\",3\r\n6112,HMG-COA REDUCTASA,HMG-CoA reductase is an enzyme that plays a crucial role in cholesterol biosynthesis and is the target of statin medications.,1\r\n6117,MIALGIAS,\"M